## 🍑 Sensory Prototyping & Taste-Memory Induction
* **Stimulus:** Consumption of a fresh nectarine.
* **Initial Response:** Generated a sharp, dual-layered neurological pleasure response localized above the hard palate (roof of the mouth). This response appears independent of the fruit's objective ripeness.
* **Induction Tracking:** 
  * Active testing confirms that conscious stimulation of the oral cavity can re-trigger the exact flavor profile of the nectarine on demand without physical stimulus.
  * **Current State Architecture:** The sensory pathway is highly localized. It originates at the front of the face and the roof of the mouth, creeps upward behind the ocular pathways (back of the eyes), and migrates toward the center of the cranium. 
